16:26.120 --> 16:26.480
actually.

16:27.580 --> 16:27.960
There's a

16:27.960 --> 16:28.380
couple of

16:28.380 --> 16:28.780
ways it

16:28.780 --> 16:29.140
can be

16:29.140 --> 16:30.060
17,

16:30.520 --> 16:31.620
and three

16:31.620 --> 16:32.120
ways I

16:32.120 --> 16:32.500
think that

16:32.500 --> 16:32.820
it can

16:32.820 --> 16:34.500
be 18,

16:35.320 --> 16:36.040
and that's

16:36.040 --> 16:36.400
the value

16:36.400 --> 16:36.980
we observe.

16:37.300 --> 16:37.920
So most of

16:37.920 --> 16:38.500
the probability

16:38.500 --> 16:39.900
is around

16:39.900 --> 16:40.520
values

16:40.520 --> 16:41.800
near the

16:41.800 --> 16:42.160
middle of

16:42.160 --> 16:42.620
the range,

16:42.680 --> 16:43.060
as we'd

16:43.060 --> 16:43.620
expect,

16:44.340 --> 16:46.160
and then we

16:46.160 --> 16:47.900
have some

16:47.900 --> 16:48.880
probability on

16:48.880 --> 16:49.880
the high values.

16:51.140 --> 16:51.940
So we

16:51.940 --> 16:52.840
actually observe

16:52.840 --> 16:53.960
the test

16:53.960 --> 16:54.800
statistic being

16:54.800 --> 16:55.880
18.

17:00.440 --> 17:01.360
In fact,

17:01.460 --> 17:02.020
there are

17:02.020 --> 17:04.260
seven

17:04.260 --> 17:06.400
ways

17:06.400 --> 17:07.220
in which

17:07.220 --> 17:07.600
the test

17:07.600 --> 17:08.700
statistic can

17:08.700 --> 17:09.640
be 18

17:09.640 --> 17:10.320
or less,

17:10.960 --> 17:11.700
and so

17:11.700 --> 17:12.680
those values

17:12.680 --> 17:13.280
collectively

17:13.280 --> 17:14.960
have probability

17:14.960 --> 17:16.000
on them

17:16.000 --> 17:18.040
of about

17:18.040 --> 17:20.680
0.055.

17:21.660 --> 17:22.740
So that's

17:22.740 --> 17:23.260
the probability

17:23.260 --> 17:24.040
of getting

17:24.040 --> 17:24.820
a value

17:24.820 --> 17:25.300
of the test

17:25.300 --> 17:25.880
statistic,

17:26.020 --> 17:26.840
WX,

17:27.640 --> 17:29.500
as inconsistent

17:29.500 --> 17:31.440
or lower,

17:31.720 --> 17:32.220
so that's

17:32.220 --> 17:33.260
18 or lower

17:33.260 --> 17:34.480
than what we

17:34.480 --> 17:35.000
observed.

17:35.260 --> 17:35.800
So 18

17:35.800 --> 17:36.280
was what we

17:36.280 --> 17:36.800
observed,

17:36.800 --> 17:37.700
and more

17:37.700 --> 17:38.360
inconsistent

17:38.360 --> 17:39.060
on the

17:39.060 --> 17:39.760
left tail

17:39.760 --> 17:40.620
would be

17:40.620 --> 17:41.160
17,

17:41.420 --> 17:41.780
16,

17:41.880 --> 17:42.320
or 15.

17:42.880 --> 17:43.460
But remember

17:43.460 --> 17:43.960
we're doing

17:43.960 --> 17:45.340
a two-sided

17:45.340 --> 17:46.640
hypothesis test

17:46.640 --> 17:47.000
here,

17:47.200 --> 17:48.460
so we need

17:48.460 --> 17:49.060
to consider

17:49.060 --> 17:50.000
the other

17:50.000 --> 17:50.720
tail too,

17:50.940 --> 17:51.780
because values

17:51.780 --> 17:52.240
at the other

17:52.240 --> 17:52.680
end of the

17:52.680 --> 17:53.220
tail would be

17:53.220 --> 17:53.540
just as

17:53.540 --> 17:54.100
inconsistent,

17:54.440 --> 17:55.480
except instead

17:55.480 --> 17:56.120
of being a lot

17:56.120 --> 17:56.620
smaller than

17:56.620 --> 17:57.200
we'd expect,

17:57.320 --> 17:57.740
they'd be

17:57.740 --> 17:58.400
larger.

17:59.080 --> 18:00.000
So we'd

18:00.000 --> 18:00.980
be considering

18:00.980 --> 18:01.900
these values

18:01.900 --> 18:02.580
0.055 as well.

18:04.020 --> 18:04.760
And by

18:04.760 --> 18:05.320
symmetry,

18:06.480 --> 18:07.200
these also

18:07.200 --> 18:07.600
have

18:07.600 --> 18:08.740
probability

18:08.740 --> 18:12.080
0.055.

18:13.000 --> 18:13.800
So that

18:13.800 --> 18:14.120
when we

18:14.120 --> 18:14.500
consider

18:14.500 --> 18:15.380
these two

18:15.380 --> 18:16.600
regions

18:16.600 --> 18:17.160
together,

18:18.740 --> 18:19.520
their combined

18:19.520 --> 18:20.100
probability,

18:20.100 --> 18:20.740
which gives

18:20.740 --> 18:21.440
the p-value

18:21.440 --> 18:22.820
for our test

18:22.820 --> 18:24.580
is approximately

18:24.580 --> 18:27.640
0.11.

18:35.700 --> 18:36.220
Hence,

18:36.600 --> 18:38.840
at the 5%

18:38.840 --> 18:39.840
significance level,

18:39.840 --> 18:49.280
there is

18:49.280 --> 18:52.300
not enough

18:52.300 --> 18:52.880
evidence

18:52.880 --> 18:59.980
to reject

18:59.980 --> 19:04.700
the null

19:04.700 --> 19:05.280
hypothesis

19:05.280 --> 19:06.020
that the

19:06.020 --> 19:06.460
two data

19:06.460 --> 19:06.920
sets are

19:06.920 --> 19:07.220
from the

19:07.220 --> 19:07.500
same

19:07.500 --> 19:08.260
distribution.

19:08.260 --> 19:09.940
Now,

19:10.300 --> 19:12.020
there may

19:12.020 --> 19:12.640
be a suspicion

19:12.640 --> 19:13.100
that if we

19:13.100 --> 19:13.320
were to

19:13.320 --> 19:13.780
gather some

19:13.780 --> 19:14.340
more data,

19:14.900 --> 19:15.600
that perhaps

19:15.600 --> 19:16.560
that picture

19:16.560 --> 19:17.300
would change,

19:17.520 --> 19:17.780
and that

19:17.780 --> 19:18.120
influence

19:18.120 --> 19:18.780
would change,

19:19.740 --> 19:20.560
and my

19:20.560 --> 19:21.140
wife might

19:21.140 --> 19:21.700
argue that

19:21.700 --> 19:22.020
we should

19:22.020 --> 19:22.520
be taking

19:22.520 --> 19:23.660
a one-sided

19:23.660 --> 19:24.400
alternative

19:24.400 --> 19:25.080
rather than

19:25.080 --> 19:25.440
a two.

19:26.160 --> 19:26.580
However,

19:27.020 --> 19:27.640
as the test

19:27.640 --> 19:28.200
would stand,

19:28.400 --> 19:28.820
we would

19:28.820 --> 19:29.560
not reject

19:29.560 --> 19:29.900
the null

19:29.900 --> 19:30.560
hypothesis.

19:30.560 --> 19:42.040
I could

19:42.040 --> 19:42.420
have used

19:42.420 --> 19:42.800
a normal

19:42.800 --> 19:43.600
approximation.

19:49.240 --> 19:49.880
Why?

19:50.360 --> 19:51.220
Because if we

19:51.220 --> 19:51.720
look at our

19:51.720 --> 19:52.520
test statistic,

19:53.760 --> 19:54.500
it's a

19:54.500 --> 19:54.900
summation,

19:54.900 --> 19:57.740
and the

19:57.740 --> 19:58.300
central limit

19:58.300 --> 19:59.200
theorem tells

19:59.200 --> 20:00.440
us that

20:00.440 --> 20:02.940
sums and

20:02.940 --> 20:05.600
averages are

20:05.600 --> 20:06.200
approximately

20:06.200 --> 20:07.180
normally distributed,

20:07.740 --> 20:08.520
at least as the

20:08.520 --> 20:09.200
sample grows

20:09.200 --> 20:09.760
large.

20:10.080 --> 20:10.660
Now, we only

20:10.660 --> 20:12.940
have a modest

20:12.940 --> 20:13.720
number of terms

20:13.720 --> 20:14.460
in the sum here,

20:14.460 --> 20:15.180
so we might not

20:15.180 --> 20:16.760
expect the normal

20:16.760 --> 20:17.580
approximation to

20:17.580 --> 20:18.240
work too well,

20:18.560 --> 20:19.280
but in any event,

20:19.360 --> 20:20.060
we have computers

20:20.060 --> 20:20.740
these days,

20:20.940 --> 20:22.140
so the computations

20:22.140 --> 20:22.720
can be quite

20:22.720 --> 20:23.360
easily done,

20:23.800 --> 20:24.240
for example,

20:24.340 --> 20:24.800
using the

20:24.800 --> 20:26.000
software R

20:26.000 --> 20:27.100
and the

20:27.100 --> 20:28.340
related command.

20:29.740 --> 20:30.520
What if we'd

20:30.520 --> 20:31.580
had ties?

20:32.000 --> 20:32.560
So what if

20:32.560 --> 20:33.020
two of the

20:33.020 --> 20:33.580
observations

20:33.580 --> 20:34.300
had been the

20:34.300 --> 20:34.640
same?

20:35.360 --> 20:35.740
Well, let's

20:35.740 --> 20:36.280
go back to

20:36.280 --> 20:36.820
our data,

20:37.980 --> 20:38.260
and let's

20:38.260 --> 20:38.920
suppose that

20:38.920 --> 20:39.460
if instead

20:39.460 --> 20:40.080
of having

20:40.080 --> 20:41.280
a score

20:41.280 --> 20:42.080
of nine

20:42.080 --> 20:42.920
here,

20:43.400 --> 20:44.220
my wife

20:44.220 --> 20:44.640
had actually

20:44.640 --> 20:45.360
